Assignment 3. JavaScript Form Validation 
• Aim: To build a robust user registration form with client-side input validation 
using JavaScript. 
• Learning Objectives: Understand form submission interception, regular 
expressions (RegEx) for data pattern matching, and real-time DOM feedback. 
• Theoretical Background: Client-side validation improves user experience by 
correcting inputs before sending them to a server. 
• Detailed Requirements: 
o Form Fields: Name (text), Email (email), Phone (tel), Password 
(password), and a Submit button. 
o Validation Rules: 
▪ Name: Cannot be empty; must contain only letters (minimum 3 
characters). 
▪ Email: Must match standard email format (use RegEx). 
▪ Phone: Must be a valid 10-digit numeric value. 
▪ Password: Minimum 8 characters, containing at least one 
uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, and one number. 
o Error Handling: Prevent default form submission if any validation fails 
(event.preventDefault()). Display specific error messages next to or below 
the respective input fields.
